import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="VolnLabs is building tools to help robotics teams establish whether a behavior change is ready to deploy, and whether that evidence still applies to the robot running it. Actryn is the first step.">
  <div class="min">
    <main id="main-content">
      <h1>Know what changed before your robot ships<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">VolnLabs is building tools to help robotics teams establish whether a behavior change is ready to deploy, and whether that evidence still applies to the robot running it.</p>

      <h2>What we build</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p><strong>Actryn is our first step.</strong> It grew from design-partner feedback asking for controlled execution that fits selected Linux environments and keeps existing driver stacks in place. It makes operation identity, authority and recovery explicit when replies are lost or systems restart.</p>
        <p><strong>AxiomOS is the research behind it.</strong> It explores the broader operating-system model for runtime-programmable robots and remains an active project.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Founder</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p><strong>Utkarsh Maurya</strong> is a systems engineer working across kernels, embedded systems and runtime correctness. He built AxiomOS and Actryn.</p>
        <p>He is also an ML research engineer at Polymath (YC W26). His prior work includes Bitcoin-only firmware for Cypherock X1 and Linux multikernel research.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="open-source">Open source</h2>
      <p>VolnLabs develops <a href="https://github.com/volnlabs/actryn">Actryn</a> and <a href="https://github.com/volnlabs/axiomos">AxiomOS</a> in public. Utkarsh has also contributed to Limine and bpftime and maintains an rbpf fork.</p>

      <h2>Programs</h2>
      <p><a href="https://claude.com/programs/startups">Claude Startups</a> · Anthropic · 2026</p>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
